// ============================================================================
// MIR-PATH MILESTONE: the JIT-EXECUTED verified `whnf_impl` WITH ITS NATIVE
// ARITHMETIC IOTA — the micro-checker's `reduce_nat_app` / `reduce_bool_app`
// (the closed-Nat ops Nat.add/sub/mul/div/mod/pow/land/lor/xor/shl/shr/beq/ble
// and Bool.beq) WIRED INTO whnf_impl via NON-EMPTY NAT_BINOPS / BOOL_BINOPS, so
// whnf's native-IOTA leaf is now FAITHFUL. THIS IS THE LAST CUT whnf reduction
// leaf: with the recursor engine already verified (Bool.rec/Nat.rec) and now the
// native ops, whnf_impl is faithful over ALL its reduction rules —
// BETA / DELTA / SPINE / ZETA + recursor-IOTA + native-IOTA.
//
// `--mir-emit-closure whnf_impl` over `native_arith_slice.rs` lowers the
// call-graph closure: whnf_impl ->
//   { reduce_nat_app -> { as_nat, nat_lit, bu_* leaves },
//     reduce_bool_app -> { as_bool, bool_const },
//     reduce_recursor -> { whnf_impl (back-edge), as_bool, nat_constructor },
//     instantiate -> subst -> lift, env_get, burn, is_* gate predicates }.
// reduce_nat_app / reduce_bool_app / as_nat / as_bool / nat_lit / bool_const /
// nat_constructor / reduce_recursor / whnf_impl are ALL REAL IN-MODULE bodies
// (verified below). Only TRUE leaves stay 0-block externs (bound below).
//
// THE HONEST CUT-LIST — the external trusted-base boundary:
//   The Nat literal payload is `BuHandle`, an OWNED thin handle to a heap
//   `num_bigint::BigUint`. The BigUint DIGIT ARITHMETIC (add/sub/mul/div/rem/
//   and/or/xor/shl/shr/pow/cmp/is_zero/from/clone) is num_bigint's own code — a
//   SEPARATE trusted base — bound as FAITHFUL `bu_*` extern leaf shims that call
//   the REAL `num_bigint::BigUint` ops (NOT toy stand-ins). What is VERIFIED
//   in-module is CLEAN's OWN control flow around them: whnf_impl's native-op
//   branch (whnf each arg, try the native rule, rebuild the spine on stuck),
//   reduce_nat_app/reduce_bool_app's op-NAME DISPATCH + the guard COMPARISONS
//   (y.is_zero(), x>=y for saturating sub, the pow/shl over-bound sentinel),
//   as_nat's constructor-CHAIN walk + nat_lit's literal construction, as_bool's
//   Bool-ctor recognition + bool_const construction. (Same pattern as the
//   recursor rung: the name_is_*/op_is_* &str-eq are leaves; the reduction LOGIC
//   is verified.)
//   Other modeled cuts (verbatim from the recursor slice): env = slice scan;
//   fuel.burn = no-op; is_* gates route to name_is_* shims (NAT_BINOPS/BOOL_BINOPS
//   NOW NON-EMPTY -> the native branch fires; RECURSORS stays non-empty -> the
//   recursor path is NOT regressed); MicroError never constructed (only the `?`
//   propagation type); Arc + BuHandle leak (drop-no-op model).
//
// We run native whnf_impl == JIT machine code over native-arith reductions:
//   - Nat.add(2,3) -> 5; Nat.mul(2,3) -> 6; Nat.sub(3,5) -> 0 (saturating);
//     Nat.succ 2 -> 3; Nat.beq(2,2) -> Bool.true; Bool.beq(true,true) -> Bool.true;
//   - a STUCK native op (a non-literal arg) -> the spine rebuilt;
//   - a NESTED `Nat.add (Nat.mul 2 3) 1` -> 7 (args whnf'd first);
//   - BOTH constructor-form Nats (succ/zero) AND Lit(BigUint) literals, to
//     exercise as_nat's two extraction paths;
//   - plus the recursor + plain BETA/DELTA/SPINE/ZETA cases (the native gate must
//     not perturb them).
//
// REGEN: `trust_ir_mir native_arith_slice.rs --crate-type=lib
//   --mir-emit-closure whnf_impl <out>`. Refresh MIR_NA_WHNF_CLOSURE_TRUST_IR AND
// the EXT_NA_* symbol constants together (the crate-disambiguator hash is in both).

