// `Ty` enum is byte-identical to the slice/production enum so rustc lays it out
// (and niche-encodes the discriminant) identically — that is what makes the
// `&Ty` thin pointer the JIT reads byte-compatible with the native value. The
// trust-ir INTERPRETER is not a usable third oracle here (it has no first-class
